# Force LF regardless of platform for anything with a shebang or that gets deployed straight to a
# Linux host - a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (this project's default) silently
# converts these to CRLF, which breaks the shebang line (#!/usr/bin/env bash\r fails) the moment
# the file is scp'd/copied to Linux as-is. Found while adding infra/proxmox-backup-encryption/'s
# scripts, which are deployed exactly that way; applies equally to every existing .sh script here
# (scripts/bring-up-tau.sh etc.), which had the identical latent risk with no .gitattributes at
# all until now.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
